# Commits and PRs (personal)

Apply these whenever creating commits or pull requests unless the user overrides them.

## Commits

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`
- Include an emoji in the **title** after the colon
- **Scope is lowercase only** (package or area name)
- No Jira key — personal work has no Jira project
- Title (first line) **must be ≤ 70 characters**
- Body is optional; keep it to why, not a file list

Examples:

```
fix(editor): 🔧 restore keybindings on Fedora
feat(cli): ✨ add json output flag
```

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`.

## Pull requests

- PR **title must match the commit title**, including the emoji
- Body: short Summary + Test plan
